Subject: [PATCH 07737/11362] [outer-loop] ARC live-search boundary: reaches
 tu93 L1 live; deep live solving is an open problem (REQ-ARC-WMTE-5840)

True live-search (StepwiseExplorer on the given env, no separate arcade) + perception
verifier: reaches tu93 L1 (both baseline and routed), but neither reaches L2/L3 even at
budget 2000 -- the offline L3 solve needs fresh_env branching (a brand-new env per node),
unavailable on a single live env (tu93 reset non-idempotent). Perception verifier adds no
advantage over the baseline explorer online. No clean idempotent nav game in the public
set for a positive demo. Honest boundary: the chain closes on the offline/dev-twin path
(tu93 L3, no hand-RE), but deep true-live solving of a non-idempotent maze is an open
research problem (parity-aware live search / world-model rollout), not a wiring gap.

